      "text": "Records\n\nWhat you see here is your record and rule-based safety information — not a diagnosis or medical advice. Discuss changes to medicines with your doctor. In an emergency call 108 / 112.\n\nYour record is yours to take\n\nDownload a FHIR R4 bundle. Drafts are excluded; the export itself is logged.\n\nExport FHIR R4 (JSON)\n🖨 Print / save as PDF\nBACKFILL FROM AN OLD PRESCRIPTION\nNothing here is a doctor's report — it is a draft until you tap confirm\nPaste text from a pharmacy or lab SMS, or photo OCR. In this build OCR is simulated: use a sample prescription\nparser confidence shown before anything is saved\nParse → save as drafts\nFILES — REPORTS, PRESCRIPTIONS, SCANS\nAES-256-GCM\nChoose a file\nDocument type\nLab report\nPrescription\nDischarge summary\nX-ray\nMRI\nCT scan\nUltrasound\nECG\nVaccination card\nBill\nOther\nTitle (optional)\nReport date (optional)\nUpload\n\nPDF, JPEG or PNG up to 3 MB; checked by content, not by name. Files are encrypted before storage and shared with doctors under full-record consent or logged emergency access. Opening normally creates an entry in your access history. Used 0 KB of 30 MB.\n\nNo files yet.\n\nTRENDS — YOUR READINGS OVER TIME\nself-reported\n\nThe shaded band is the target range. These readings are what you log yourself between visits — they show the journey, and they are never a diagnosis.\n\nLog a reading\n\nFrom your glucometer, BP monitor or diary. Self-reported — a data point, not a diagnosis.\n\nWhat are you logging?\nFasting glucose (mg/dL)\nPost-meal glucose (mg/dL)\nHbA1c (%)\nBP systolic (mmHg)\nBP diastolic (mmHg)\nPeak flow (L/min)\nWeight (kg)\nSave reading\nYour last readings\n\nRemove an entry that was a mistake — every change is in your audit trail.\n\nNothing logged yet.\n\nTIMELINE\n\nNo visits or lab results are recorded yet.\n\nMEDICINES\n\nNo medicines recorded.\n\nALLERGIES & CONDITIONS\n\nNone recorded.",
